_Langwirksame_Insulinanaloga_zur_Behandlung_des_Diabetes_mellitus_Typ_2.pdf</ext-link>, accessed 17 December 2007</citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mullins</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharplin</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Yki-J&#x000e4;rvinen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Riddle</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>H&#x000e4;ring</surname><given-names>HU</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Negative binomial meta-regression of combined HbA<sub>1c</sub> and hypoglycemia across eleven phase III and IV studies of insulin glargine compared with NPH insulin in type 1 and type 2 diabetes</article-title><source>Clin Ther</source><year>2007</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>1607</fpage><lpage>1619</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.clinthera.2007.08.020</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Mullins P, Sharplin P, Yki-J&#x000e4;rvinen H, Riddle MC, H&#x000e4;ring HU (2007) Negative binomial meta-regression of combined HbA1c and hypoglycemia across eleven phase III and IV studies of insulin glargine compared with NPH insulin in type 1 and type 2 diabetes. Clin Ther 29:1607&#x02013;1619 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17919543</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Alonso</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hypoglycemia as a barrier to glycemic control</article-title><source>J Diabet Complicat</source><year>2004</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>60</fpage><lpage>68</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1056-8727(03)00058-8</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Davis S, Alonso MD (2004) H